{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nThe sibling emitter writes candidate fixture specs asserting a criterion should fire or stay\nsilent for a real plan. Those assertions come from history, not current code, so a candidate that\ndisagrees with today's criterion is unseparably either wrong or evidence the criterion drifted.\nAdmitting an unverified candidate is worse than none: a wrong must-fire case encodes a false\npositive as required behavior. One run cannot settle it — of 551 store review pairs over\nbyte-identical material, 208 flipped verdict, which is why shipped specs use `epochs: 3` with\n`gate: at_least(2)`.\n\n## Approach\n\nRun each candidate against current code before admitting it; keep disagreements as evidence.\n\n**Run.** The emitter writes one strict-valid candidate spec per criterion, each a `dataset` whose cases carry an `expect` of `finding` or `pass`. For each case the runner executes the\ncriterion's real Pass-1 finder via `eval_solver.run_case(prompt_id, case, runner=live,\nrepo_root=repo_root)` (`eval_solver.py:322`; `runner`/`repo_root` keyword-only). It does NOT call\n`calibrate_criterion`, which only scores a persisted dataset (`load_eval_spec`, `eval.py:69-78`);\nthis run targets criteria with no existing spec. Each case runs three times; `_fired(verdict)` (a\nfinding present) gives the observed verdict; a case matching its `expect` in ≥2 of 3 runs\nREPRODUCES.\n\n**Disposition.** A reproducing case is kept; a non-reproducing case is withheld to a drift report\nat `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/fixtures/drift-report.md` recording criterion, predicted vs\nobserved behavior, and originating review. To write a criterion's spec the runner carries the\ncandidate's strict-only fields — `prompt`, `model`, `epochs`, `gate`, `coverage_threshold`,\n`scorers` (the deterministic gating scorer) — through UNCHANGED, and rebuilds BOTH `dataset` and\n`gold_set` (the emitter's 1:1 input/label projection of the dataset) from only that criterion's\nreproducing cases. The spec lands at `.rebar/evals/<prompt-id>.eval.yaml` only when the filtered\ndataset is balanced (both-sides-non-empty) with a non-empty `gold_set` and\n`validate_eval_spec(spec, strict=True)` returns zero errors — strict requires exactly that\nnon-empty gold_set and the ≥1 deterministic gating scorer these carried fields supply; otherwise\nthe whole criterion is withheld to the drift report. The\nspec carries NO posture field: posture is a routing concept (`default_posture` in\n`criteria_routing.json`), not eval-spec schema; the selector's tier is recorded in the admission\nreport, never on the spec.\n\n**No-shadowing guard.** A user `.rebar/evals/<id>.eval.yaml` WINS over a packaged built-in at load\n(`eval_spec_path` before `_packaged_eval_spec`), so a colliding mined spec would silently shadow a\nbuilt-in. The runner therefore SKIPS any criterion whose `<prompt-id>.eval.yaml` already exists in\npackaged `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/` or as a `.rebar/evals/` file.\n\n**Budget enforcement.** Before each criterion the run pre-flights through\n`ledger.reserve(estimate_usd, ledger_path=<epic ledger>, cap_usd=250.0, reserve_usd=0.0)` against\nthis epic's own `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/fixtures/ledger.jsonl` (reserve_usd=0 makes the\nceiling exactly $250), then `finalize()`s\npriced ACTUAL usage per criterion. Because `finalize` prices real tokens that can exceed the\nestimate, after EACH `finalize` the run re-reads cumulative actual spend from that ledger and, if\nit now meets or exceeds `cap_usd`, halts FATALLY before any further criterion — so $250 bounds\nactual finalized spend, not just estimates. The estimate key comes from the criterion's `exec` tier\nin `criteria.effective_routing('.', gate_key='plan_review')`: `AGENT`→`criteria-eval-agent`,\n`1-TURN`/`2-STEP`→`criteria-eval-cheap` (`exec: DET` is out of scope — stripped before `pass1_chunk`\nper ADR 0033; `exec_tier` never returns DET). Model parity is pinned to the\nproduction Pass-1 class per ADR 0109.\n\n**Failure disposition.** A criterion is atomic: spec written and spend `finalize()`d only after all\nits cases finish three runs — no partial criterion lands. A transient model/transport error is\nRETRYABLE (three attempts, exponential backoff), then the criterion is left uncompleted (no spec;\nrun continues). Both a pre-flight `reserve` `BudgetExceeded` and the\npost-`finalize` cumulative-actual cap breach are FATAL/non-retryable and stop the run with all\nfinalized criteria admitted. Each criterion finalizes under a stable\n`run_id = f\"admission-{prompt_id}\"`, so a re-run resumes at the first criterion absent from the\nledger and `reconcile` recharges none already recorded.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe admission runner, its disposition logic, the drift-report writer, and the `.rebar/evals/` specs.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Repairing drift (each entry becomes a follow-on ticket linked `discovered_from` the epic);\n  editing `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/`; scheduling re-runs (the sibling self-healing loop owns that).\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tests drive the disposition logic through a stubbed solver returning scripted\nfire/no-fire sequences (deterministic, no model); every Acceptance Criterion below names its\ncase and check. One live run exercises the real path end to end.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A must-fire case with scripted runs (fire, fire, silent) is admitted into its criterion's\n      written dataset (`pytest`).\n- [ ] A must-fire case with scripted runs (fire, silent, silent) is withheld and writes a\n      drift-report entry naming criterion, predicted/observed behavior, and originating review\n      (`pytest`).\n- [ ] When the ledger already holds spend leaving no room under the ceiling, the first criterion's\n      `reserve` raises `BudgetExceeded` and a call-counting stub reports `0` model calls (`pytest`).\n- [ ] When a criterion's finalized ACTUAL spend pushes cumulative ledger spend to or past\n      `cap_usd`, the run halts before the next criterion (the breaching one stays admitted);\n      `pytest` uses synthetic rows whose priced usd exceeds the estimate and a call-counting stub\n      reports no next-criterion calls.\n- [ ] Every written spec returns zero errors from `validate_eval_spec(spec, strict=True)`; `pytest`\n      invokes the real validator over each written file.\n- [ ] A criterion whose `<prompt-id>.eval.yaml` matches a packaged built-in in\n      `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/` is skipped; written and packaged basenames intersect emptily\n      (`pytest`).\n- [ ] A criterion whose reproducing cases leave one side empty writes no spec and records its cases\n      in the drift report (`pytest`).\n- [ ] A criterion whose cases raise before all finish writes no partial `.eval.yaml`; verified by\n      `pytest`, after a mid-criterion failure.\n- [ ] A re-run after a fatal stop recharges no already-finalized criterion; `pytest` asserts\n      `reconcile` returns the existing row for a completed `run_id`, zero new calls.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] A live admission run has completed over the full candidate set with the Pass-1\n      model pinned to its production class, and this epic's ledger records total spend greater than\n      zero and at most 250.0 with a per-pass model id on every row.\n      provenance: environment=developer workstation against the production Bedrock chain;\n      principal=the configured Bedrock plan-review identity; privilege_posture=production-equivalent;\n      instrument=live-call — real Pass-1 behavior no offline analysis substitutes for.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] Each drift-report entry has a corresponding ticket linked `discovered_from`\n      the parent epic.\n      provenance: environment=the rebar tickets store; principal=the session's configured rebar\n      assignee; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — a store write.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n`make lint`/`make typecheck`/`make test` pass; the live run completed; drift report and admitted\nspecs committed; cumulative actual ledger spend ≤ $250 (reserve_usd=0 plus the post-finalize halt).\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788420943233328001,"uuid":"df7191d6-09ee-4e6b-9b49-9e518cbeb375"}